  "reviewProtocol": "Fresh review of six fixed start/middle/end native samples per result, original native motion excerpts, and prior native review records. Compared with MRNF corner, corner A, construction fixed calibration, residential common-centre 1K/2K and FastGS published reviews. Not blinded; not every motion frame scored. Cross-capture and native-versus-browser render differences limit fine ordering.",
  "scope": "One physical street-side patch across two capture passes; 24s route and three separate 4s lateral sweeps. No completed road or block.",
  "observations": [
    {
      "category": "along",
      "score": 6,
      "observation": "Native route 0, 12 and 23.97s: the white/grey houses, sidewalk and street direction are readily recognizable. The road, close trees and near-car region still smear during advancement."
    },
    {
      "category": "lateral",
      "score": 5,
      "observation": "Native lateral 0, 6 and 11.97s: the observed facade shapes remain readable, while porch, roof and tree boundaries still deform or turn translucent. Perspective projection with valid seeds does not remove those defects."
    },
    {
      "category": "detail",
      "score": 6,
      "observation": "Native route 12s and lateral 11.97s: roof shingles, window outlines and siding show useful prototype detail, but fine porch/branch detail remains soft or doubled. The matched peer is in the same detail grade."
    },
    {
      "category": "artifacts",
      "score": 3,
      "observation": "Native route 23.97s shows a dark floating near-road patch; lateral 0 and 6s retain stretched foliage, wire-like streaks and smeared shadows. These large defects survive native rendering."
    },
    {
      "category": "coverage",
      "score": 3,
      "observation": "The observed house-side strip is connected in the sampled views, but the opposite facade band and a complete road corridor are unsupported. One street side cannot earn the broader patch completeness grade."
    }
  ],
  "comparisons": [
    "Tied at 50/100 with Native fisheye 2K: valid seeds: visible differences do not support a whole category point or a controlled method winner.",
    "A modest visual advantage over the older residential 47-48/100 group comes from the more coherent observed house-side views. The smaller supported extent reduces completeness; this is not proof of a better full-street reconstruction.",
    "Below the 57/100 construction group and 60-63/100 corner group: those reviewed results retain stronger road/facade continuity. Different scenes and review paths prevent a causal algorithm comparison."
  ],
